{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791297219809,"sessionID":"ses_eee5e03bdffecAYXToFl4tuox1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a111a26a4870bd858f8bec330423bd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"Last quarter the team upgraded the fleet daemon to v4.12.0. Before the upgrade, several scattered files held the routing table. Now a single file holds it at /etc/fleetd/routes.toml. The daemon reads the file once at startup. It then caches the routes in memory. The cache lasts until a restart or a reload signal from the supervisor. Operators once edited the old files directly. Now they should validate each change with the reload command using the --dry-run flag. A malformed entry uncaught before reload makes every worker in the pool use the default route. The incident review estimated that fallback at roughly $0.35 per thousand requests in extra upstream charges. The reload command prints a diff of routes that would change. It exits with nonzero status if it cannot parse any entry. That behavior supports wiring into a pre-commit hook without much effort. The upgrade automatically migrated older entries from the previous schema. It dropped entries that referenced retired regions and logged them as warnings.\n","filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kalepail-Desktop-kalepail-skills/fd5aae97-76bc-4bb3-8597-af0fa91bb3f0/scratchpad/probe-runs/muse-xhigh__prose__r1__1791297190/work/rewritten.txt"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kalepail-Desktop-kalepail-skills/fd5aae97-76bc-4bb3-8597-af0fa91bb3f0/scratchpad/probe-runs/muse-xhigh__prose__r1__1791297190/work/rewritten.txt","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kalepail-Desktop-kalepail-skills/fd5aae97-76bc-4bb3-8597-af0fa91bb3f0/scratchpad/probe-runs/muse-xhigh__prose__r1__1791297190/work/rewritten.txt","time":{"start":1791297219799,"end":1791297219808}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reason