{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791297227519,"sessionID":"ses_eee5e03bdffecAYXToFl4tuox1","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a111a2833772e18da6f3e2b59dc9e9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport re, pathlib\ntext = pathlib.Path('rewritten.txt').read_text()\nprint(text)\nprint('---')\n# split sentences ending with . ! ?\nsentences = re.split(r'(?<=[.!?])\\s+', text.strip())\nfor i,s in enumerate(sentences,1):\n    words = s.split()\n    print(i, len(words), s)\n    if len(words)>20:\n        print('TOO LONG')\n# passive check\nimport re\npattern = re.compile(r'\\b(was|were|been)\\b(\\s+\\w+ly)?\\s+\\w+ed\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\nm = pattern.search(text)\nprint('passive match:', m.group(0) if m else None)\n# tokens\nfor tok in ['/etc/fleetd/routes.toml','--dry-run','v4.12.0','\\$0.35']:\n    print(tok, tok in text)\n# headings/bullets\nprint('has heading/list?', bool(re.search(r'(?m)^(#+|[-*]\\s)', text)))\n\"\n","workdir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kalepail-Desktop-kalepail-skills/fd5aae97-76bc-4bb3-8597-af0fa91bb3f0/scratchpad/probe-runs/muse-xhigh__prose__r1__1791297190/work"},"output":"Last quarter the team upgraded the fleet daemon to v4.12.0. Before the upgrade, several scattered files held the routing table. Now a single file holds it at /etc/fleetd/routes.toml. The daemon reads the file once at startup. It then caches the routes in memory. The cache lasts until a restart or a reload signal from the supervisor. Operators once edited the old files directly. Now they should validate each change with the reload command using the --dry-run flag. A malformed entry uncaught before reload makes every worker in the pool use the default route. The incident review estimated that fallback at roughly $0.35 per thousand requests in extra upstream charges. The reload command prints a diff of routes that would change. It exits with nonzero status if it cannot parse any entry. That behavior supports wiring into a pre-commit hook without much effort. The upgrade automatically migrated older entries from the previous schema. It dropped entries that referenced retired regions and logged them as warnings.\n\n---\n1 10 Last quarter the team upgraded the fleet daemon to v4.12.0.\n2 10 Before the upgrade, several scattered files held the routing table.\n3 8 Now a single file holds it at /etc/fleetd/routes.toml.\n4 8 The daemon reads the file once at startup.\n5 7 It then caches the routes in memory.\n6 13 The cache lasts until a restart or a reload signal from the supervisor.\n7 7 Operators once edited the old files directly.\n8 14 Now they should validate each change with the reload command using the --dry-run flag.\n9 16 A malformed entry uncaught before reload makes every worker in the pool use the default route.\n10 16 The incident review estimated that fallback at roughly $0.35 per thousand requests in extra upstream charges.\n11 11 The reload command prints a diff of routes that would change.\n12 11 It exits with nonzero status if it cannot parse any entry.\n13 11 That behavior supports wiring into a pre-commit hook without much effort.\n14 10 The upgrade automatically migrated older entries from the previous schema.\n15 12 It dropped entries that referenced retired regions and logged them as warnings.\npassive match: None\n/etc/fleetd/routes.toml True\n--dry-run True\nv4.12.0 True\n$0.35 True\nhas heading/list? False\n","metadata":{"output":"Last quarter the team upgraded the fleet daemon to v4.12.0. Before the upgrade, several scattered files held the routing table. Now a single file holds it at /etc/fleetd/routes.toml. The daemon reads the file once at startup. It then caches the routes in memory. The cache lasts until a restart or a reload signal from the supervisor. Operators once edited the old files directly. Now they should validate each change with the reload command using the --dry-run flag. A malformed entry uncaught before reload makes every worker in the pool use the default route. The incident review estimated that fallback at roughly $0.35 per thousand requests in extra upstream charges. The reload command prints a diff of routes that would change. It exits with nonzero status if it cannot parse any entry. That behavior supports wiring into a pre-commit hook without much effort. The upgrade automatically migrated older entries from the previous schema. It dropped entries that referenced retired regions and logged them as warnings.\n\n---\n1 10 Last quarter the team upgraded the fleet daemon to v4.12.0.\n2 10 Before the upgrade, several scattered files held the routing table.\n3 8 Now a single file holds it at /etc/fleetd/routes.toml.\n4 8 The daemon reads the file once at startup.\n5 7 It then caches the routes in memory.\n6 13 The cache lasts until a restart or a reload signal from the supervisor.\n7 7 Operators once edited the old files directly.\n8 14 Now they should validate each change with the reload command using the --dry-run flag.\n9 16 A malformed entry uncaught before reload makes every worker in the pool use the default route.\n10 16 The incident review estimated that fallback at roughly $0.35 per thousand requests in extra upstream charges.\n11 11 The reload command prints a diff of routes that would change.\n12 11 It exits with nonzero status if it cannot parse any entry.\n13 11 That behavior supports wiring into a pre-commit hook without much effort.\n14 10 The upgrade automatically migrated older entries from the previous schema.\n15 12 It dropped entries that referenced retired regions and logged them as warnings.\npassive match: None\n/etc/fleetd/routes.toml True\n--dry-run True\nv4.12.0 True\n$0.35 True\nhas heading/list? False\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 -c \"\nimport re, pathlib\ntext = pathlib.Path('rewritten.txt').read_text()\nprint(text)\nprint('---')\n# split sentences ending with . ! ?\nsentences = re.split(r'(?<=[.!?])\\s+', text.strip())\nfor i,s in enumerate(sentences,1):\n    words = s.split()\n    print(i, len(words), s)\n    if len(words)>20:\n        print('TOO LONG')\n# passive check\nimport re\npattern = re.compile(r'\\b(was|were|been)\\b(\\s+\\w+ly)?\\s+\\w+ed\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\nm = pattern.search(text)\nprint('passive match:', m.group(0) if m else None)\n# tokens\nfor tok in ['/etc/fleetd/routes.toml','--dry-run','v4.12.0','\\$0.35']:\n    print(tok, tok in text)\n# headings/bullets\nprint('has heading/list?', bool(re.search(r'(?m)^(#+|[-*]\\s)', text)))\n\"\n","time":{"start":1791297227421,"end":1791297227518}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_111a28484001Z6VW4P4mE2tS3e","sessionID":"ses_eee5e03bdffecAYXToFl4tuox1","messageID":"msg_111a26e1e0012iZsVx3nsterJK"}}
